e plan records rather than backend motion, which is exactly why the promise is only uncertain.","scientific_promise":"uncertain","step":0.05,"stopping_conditions":["Stop the batch after max_candidates = 6 coordinate candidates or when the planned_budget (24 tool calls, 6 backend solves, 5940 s wall, 0 workers) is exhausted, whichever comes first.","Stop early and report success only if a candidate yields joint_reach_holding_acceptance true (holding position and speed inside the recorded limits and terminal reach retained), verified by the frozen acceptance comparison rather than by raw weighted cost.","Stop a candidate immediately on any force-bound violation, solver error, non-finite state, or invalid/incomplete execution; record it as a constraint failure rather than a physical result.","Stop and report separability as unresolved if deadline_misses remains 35 of 35 and effective_horizon stays truncated below the configured horizon 10, since weight-only coordinates then cannot be separated from compute-budget/horizon truncation.","Halt a candidate after at most two bounded provider attempts on transport failure; a transport failure is not evidence about the hypothesis.","Terminate this stage without executing any batch or promoting any candidate: a validated plan requires a future grant."],"variables":{"control/recipe/holding_tip_speed_weight":[0.0001,1.0],"control/recipe/terminal_tip_speed_weight":[0.0,1.0]},"verification":["candidate.apply","simulation.run","evaluation.run","control.profile_report","bound_comparison","diagnostic_revision"],"version":"1.0.0","weakening_observations":["The single executed weight change (holding_tip_speed_weight 0.0->0.05, F462 -> F538) moved the sampled holding max speed by only -0.4060100069642385 m/s (F301) from 1.5810152739742807 (F58) to 1.1750052670100422 (F160), still about 59x the 0.02 m/s limit (F440); a coordinate increase in the same weight may therefore be low-yield rather than settling the failure.","The same change wor